# Mirrors .gitignore's spirit for the Docker build context. Unlike
# .gitignore, a BARE pattern here (no "**/" prefix) only matches at the
# build context ROOT, not at any depth — an earlier version of this file
# used bare patterns for .env/.env.test/.env.production, which did NOT
# exclude apps/api/.env (real secrets, including this project's own
# generated production secrets) and they ended up baked directly inside
# a built image layer. Found by actually inspecting a built image's
# contents (`docker run ... ls apps/api/.env*`), not by reading this
# file back. Every pattern below that needs to match at any depth (most
# of them — this repo has per-package .env/dist/node_modules/etc, not
# just root-level ones) now explicitly uses "**/".

**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

**/dist/
**/build/
**/.next/
**/out/

.turbo/

.git/
.github/

**/.env
**/.env.test
**/.env.production
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*

**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

**/coverage/

# Root-level runtime uploads directory ONLY (DOCUMENT_STORAGE_PATH/
# PAYSLIP_STORAGE_PATH) — anchored with a leading slash so this does NOT
# also match apps/api/src/common/storage/, which is real source code
# (StorageService interface + LocalDiskStorageService). An earlier,
# unanchored "**/storage/" pattern here matched that source directory
# too and broke the build with "Cannot find module" errors — found
# immediately by actually running `docker build`, not by inspection.
/storage/

**/*.tsbuildinfo

**/*.md
!README.md
